    "type": "single",
    "prompt": "Which statement best characterizes the concept of ‘security through obscurity’?",
    "scenario": "<div class=\"scenario-text\"><p>A development team asserts that their administrative interface is secure solely because the URL path is not published or linked from the public site.</p></div>",
    "options": [
      { "id": "a", "text": "A recommended primary strategy that replaces the need for authentication and encryption" },
      { "id": "b", "text": "A weak approach that relies on secrecy of design or location rather than robust controls" },
      { "id": "c", "text": "An industry best practice endorsed by NIST and ISO 27001 as a standalone control" },
      { "id": "d", "text": "The practice of making all source code and architecture diagrams publicly available" }
    ],
    "correct": ["b"],
    "explanation": "Security through obscurity depends on keeping the existence or location of a system secret. It is widely regarded as insufficient when used as the primary or sole protective measure."
